meta {
  name: Get Bulk Email
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

get {
  url: {{notificationsBaseUrl}}/api/v1/notifications/bulk-email/{{bulkEmailJobGuid}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

vars:pre-request {
  bulkEmailJobGuid: e6c63664-de00-415a-b0a1-9fb5ac3fba8e
}

docs {
  One bulk job in full: the list-row summary plus the rendered bodyHtml, attachment
  metadata, lastError, and a computed pendingCount. Job-level only — it does not
  enumerate recipients (use Get Bulk Email Recipients for that).
  
  Set bulkEmailJobGuid from a List Bulk Emails response, or from the jobGuid the
  create call returned.
  
  Path param bulkEmailJobGuid is route-constrained to a GUID. A non-GUID segment is a
  route miss (bare 404, handler never runs).
  
  Success (200): data is a BulkEmailJobDetailDto:
    jobGuid, subject, bodyHtml, status,
    totalRecipients, sentCount, failedCount, suppressedCount,
    pendingCount (= totalRecipients - sent - failed - suppressed, i.e. Queued+Sending),
    attachmentMode (None | Link | Attach), attachmentFileName, attachmentContentType,
    lastError, createdDate, startedDate, completedDate.
  
  lastError here is only set when recipient RESOLUTION threw (an Employee selection, or
  the Students service unreachable). Per-recipient send errors are on the recipient row,
  not here — see Get Bulk Email Recipients.
  
  404 not_found "Bulk email not found." - no BulkEmailJobs row with that GUID. This also
  covers a GUID that belongs to a transactional OutboundEmails row (an OTP): the join
  finds nothing, so those are structurally unreachable here.
  401 unauthorized - no valid erp_access cookie.
}
